<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan central bank injects T$9.5 bln in fund.</title>
<headline>Taiwan central bank injects T$9.5 bln in fund.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's central bank injected T$9.5 billion worth of funds into the banking system through open market operations on Tuesday, a central bank official said.</p>
<p>The bank executed a repurchase of negotiable certificates of deposit, treasury bills and government bonds offered by interested financial institutions with a rate of 7.15 percent.</p>
<p>The institutions have the option of repurchasing the NCDs, treasury bills and government bonds within 14 days, the official said.  </p>
